---
name: RBAC — permissions required for every new feature
description: Enforces that every new page, API route, or server action includes proper RBAC permission wiring
globs:
  - app/(dashboard)/**/*.tsx
  - app/api/**/*.ts
  - app/actions/*.ts
alwaysApply: true
---

## RBAC rules — always follow these when creating or editing features

### New page (app/(dashboard)/**page.tsx)
1. Add a permission to `lib/permissions.ts` if one doesn't exist yet:
   - Format: `"resource:action"` e.g. `"invoices:view"`, `"invoices:manage"`
   - Add to the PERMISSIONS object AND the Permission type
   - Add a human label to PERMISSION_LABELS
   - Add a Greek description to PERMISSION_DESCRIPTIONS
2. Add the permission to DEFAULT_ROLE_PERMISSIONS in `lib/permissions.ts` for the relevant roles
3. Add `requireAdminRoute(user, PERMISSIONS.YOUR_PERMISSION)` at the top of the page server component
4. If the page should appear in the sidebar, add a nav item with `requiresPermission: PERMISSIONS.YOUR_PERMISSION` in `lib/nav-config.ts`
5. Run `npx tsx scripts/sync-airtable-role-options.ts` is NOT needed for permissions — only for new role slugs

### New API route (app/api/**route.ts)
1. Always start every handler with:
```ts
   const session = await getSessionFromCookies()
   if (!session) return Response.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 })
   if (!hasPermission(session, PERMISSIONS.YOUR_PERMISSION)) return Response.json({ error: 'Forbidden' }, { status: 403 })
```
2. Use an existing permission if one covers the resource, or add a new one following the page rules above
3. Never use raw `user.role === "admin"` checks — always use `hasPermission()`

### New server action (app/actions/*.ts)
1. Always start with `requireAccountsPermission()` pattern or inline:
```ts
   const user = await getSessionFromCookies()
   if (!user) redirect(ROUTES.login)
   if (!hasPermission(user, PERMISSIONS.YOUR_PERMISSION)) redirect(ROUTES.dashboard)
```
2. Never use raw role checks

### Adding permission to DEFAULT_ROLE_PERMISSIONS
- admin → always include all permissions (admin has ALL_PERMISSIONS)
- manager → include unless it's a destructive/config permission
- chatter → only if chatters genuinely need this feature
- virtual_assistant → only if VAs genuinely need this feature  
- model → only if models need it
- client → only if clients need it

### Checklist before committing any new feature
- [ ] Permission added to PERMISSIONS object in lib/permissions.ts
- [ ] Permission added to PERMISSION_LABELS and PERMISSION_DESCRIPTIONS
- [ ] Permission added to correct roles in DEFAULT_ROLE_PERMISSIONS
- [ ] Page guard uses requireAdminRoute() or hasPermission()
- [ ] API route returns 401 (no session) and 403 (no permission)
- [ ] Nav item has requiresPermission if page should be in sidebar
- [ ] No raw user.role === "..." checks added
